kdm sm_86
# Every arrangement of primitives that produces an operator, and what each costs this part.
# Found from the relations alone. No ruleset, no machine file and no naming went into a row
# here. A cost is an exact rational, numerator/denominator in the part's clock count, and a cost
# of - over 0 runs has not been timed on anything.
#
# The rows of an operator are in no order. Timed in the order they were found, a chain's
# reading carries where it sat and not what it costs; shuffled, that washes out over runs and
# what is left is the difference between the arrangements. The order moves whenever a run is
# folded in, which is why it moves and a cost does not.

# operator	nodes	chain	cost	runs
